Based on discussions with CyberArk, they have identified a potential solution in which the Salesforce (SF) local account is configured to leverage a SAML-based authentication model. In this design, Salesforce would act as the primary Service Identity Provider, while CyberArk would initiate the authentication flow and pass the SAMLResponse as the user identity during sign-on.
 
Should CyberArk confirm that this approach is fully supported and technically viable, we could have your team provision a test dedicated local Salesforce account with the (PR MFA) method and enforce an Identity Policy requiring one of the organization's approved phishing-resistant MFA methods.
 
