This usecase also require setting up a policy dedicated to use passkey as its anti-phishing authentication method.
This policy will be assigned to each CLMadmin setup and same setup with each salesforce web - SAML provisioning app

Each of the CLMAdmin will have its own SP entity ID from the salesforce side configured to do SAML directly to the app from CyberArk Access tile. e.g. jaime.my.salesforce.com

Now the users to use each of the CLMAdmin app will be bundled into an identity role, this role will be assigned to each CLAdmin app so they can have access to each of the apps

Once they click on the SF CLAdmin app, the option to prompt users to setup a passkey on login will be enabled at policy level so they can setup passkey with their Laptop
Once setup, the enrolled passkey will serve for all the CLAdmin application.

